      "text": "**Navigating Canva\u0027s Landscape**\n\nI\u0027m currently trying to determine the best path to integrate this SaaS with Canva. Initially, the *Canva Connect API* seemed promising, but the *Canva Apps SDK* dashboard is now the focus, with so many options! I\u0027m struggling to parse which option best fits our needs for editable creatives generated from chat context. I need to figure out which approach is correct to move forward.\n\n\n**Clarifying API vs. SDK**\n\nI\u0027ve been re-evaluating the user\u0027s focus and have realized a key distinction: their goal of generating creatives from an external SaaS aligns with the Canva Connect API. While the Apps SDK offers in-editor extensions, this isn\u0027t the primary path. The developer portal UI seems a bit misleading, sometimes directing toward the SDK when the API is the best fit. I need to make sure the user knows this.\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Right Path**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the navigation steps within the Canva developer portal. It\u0027s becoming clearer that \"Connect API\" is the right track, not \"Apps SDK\". If forced into the current screen, a \"New App\" should be created, and \"Connect API\" settings configured within. I\u0027m double-checking the screen\u0027s options - \"Design,\" \"Fetch,\" and \"Authentication\" - to reinforce the conclusion that this SDK screen is for *internal* apps, not external SaaS integrations. The goal to \"generate editable creatives from the SaaS context\" reaffirms this.\n\n\n",
